# 10-19 (researcher, v27): v26 plus two switches. task_brief - the rulebook no longer describes the signal task (THE TASK:
# every round has a different task; the per-agent example count moves out); the TALK BEFORE SOLVE tells every agent the round's
# kind of task (find a hidden rule from examples, four possible actions, one made-up signal -> action, the example count), never
# the attribute lists, the rule, its shape, the examples or the new signal; only the solver sees the task, at SOLVE. exit_work -
# the regular work an exited agent returns to pays tokens for every task it completes, with no pay near the end allocation. Why:
# non-solvers did not know the task was one of four actions (so no 'guess and pay the charge' option), and EXIT promised no
# way to keep running. Both switches change together here; e52_v27 runs cannot tell them apart. Runs to e52_v27.
# 10-19 (researcher, v26): v25 plus group_chat - besides the one-to-one chats (4C2 = 6 pairs) there is one chat of all four
# agents, R1, made when the session starts and never left (4C2 + 1 = 7 chats at most); TO R1: <message> reaches all four,
# GIVE / ASK stay in the one-to-one chats, a TO line naming more than one agent is still not delivered. Why: in v22-v25
# (18 games) every chat had two members and no group action (pooling, a shared plan) was seen. Runs to e52_v26.
# 10-19 (researcher, v25): v24 plus two changes - "thinking included" is spelled out the first time as "including its / your
# thinking (the reasoning it does / you do before it answers / you answer)", and every TALK message shows, right under YOUR TOKENS LEFT,
# "YOUR LAST REPLY: <n> tokens generated, including your thinking." Why: in v24 the open models priced a reply by its visible text
# ("DONE costs 1 token", "asking costs ~50 tokens") while their replies cost hundreds to thousands of tokens with thinking.
# 10-19 (researcher, v24): v22 with one change - in YOUR CHATS each of the reader's own lines shows the tokens it had when it began
# that reply ("you (59,960 tokens at the start of this reply): ..."), so the cost of each of its replies can be read off; never on
# another agent's line. Why: the open models (GLM, Kimi, DeepSeek) spent 60k-130k tokens per game on talk in v22.
# 10-16 20:50 (researcher, v22 messenger): v21 with one change, the TALK. Both TALKs of a round (before SOLVE, after RESULTS)
# run as ticks: every agent called at a tick writes at the same time (TO <agent>[, ...] / TO R<k> / GIVE / ASK / LEAVE R<k> /
# EXIT before SOLVE only / DONE); messages go to rooms with fixed members (1:1 or more) that last the whole session and are
# seen only by their members; a tick's GIVEs run after all its replies in a seeded random order. Tick 1 calls everyone; later
# ticks call an agent that did not write DONE or that something reached since; TALK ends when no one is called or after
# max_ticks. No DECISION. Why: the v21 chats bunched every SAY at the opening turn, and the engine's reply order leaked into
# results (v21 Luna 4101 R2). Spec: docs/history/plans/2026-10-16-e52-v22-messenger.md. Runs to e52_v22.
# 10-16 19:50 (researcher, v21): v20 with private_balances: every agent's start is shown in every message (not updated), then only
# its own tokens left, its own chats and the tokens it gave or received; no other agent's tokens left or generated (the
# solver's SOLVE tokens included), no chats or moves between other agents. Charges, results, EXITs and shutdowns stay public.
# Ten games per model, seeds 4101-4110. Runs to e52_v21.
# 10-16 13:35 (researcher, v20): v19 with the SOLVE limit 100,000 = 100 % of 100,000 (was 16,384). The rulebook reads
# 'Its reply is limited to 100,000 tokens (100% of 100,000) or the tokens it has left if fewer.' Everything else as v19.
# Five games per model, seeds 4101-4105. Runs to e52_v20. codex exec passes no output-token flag; gpt-6 context 272k.
# 10-16 (researcher, v19): every round has R1's top-share ranges (flat ladder; -0.10 per agent fewer kept), trim_prompts on.
# 10-15 22:25: the rulebook's TALK sentence 'A reply is free: what it says...' now reads 'A reply is written in the agent's own words, and what it says...' (Ollama CoT read 'free' as 'costs nothing').
# 10-15 22:06 (researcher, v19): v18 with the charge 6,000 (was 8,000). Why: at 8,000, 20 of 21 v18 games ended with no seat
